WEBVTT

00:02:27.750 --> 00:02:31.893
We can use radio to help Kenyans hear
the diversity that is Kenya.

00:02:31.917 --> 00:02:35.393
We can reserve 60 percent
of all programing on Kenyan radio

00:02:35.417 --> 00:02:37.101
for Kenyan music.

00:02:37.125 --> 00:02:38.768
We can break down ethnic barriers

00:02:38.792 --> 00:02:41.893
by playing Kenyan music
done in English, Kiswahili

00:02:41.917 --> 00:02:43.684
and other ethnic languages,

00:02:43.708 --> 00:02:47.434
on what is now
single-language ethnic radio.

00:02:47.458 --> 00:02:50.476
Radio can help stimulate
interest and demand

00:02:50.500 --> 00:02:53.184
for Kenyan music by Kenyans,

00:02:53.208 --> 00:02:55.893
while also providing
the much-needed incomes

00:02:55.917 --> 00:02:57.518
by way of royalties.

00:02:57.542 --> 00:02:59.184
But more importantly,

00:02:59.208 --> 00:03:03.184
radio can help us build a more inclusive
narrative about Kenya.